# DEFORM-FIELD: the deformation field around the main view (Notion DEFORM-ARCH card 1). A script presses the
# DeformStamp asset DS_CircleRim three times along a line in FIELD_Barn; the debug view "Deformation Field" shows the
# field over the scene (blue = sink, red = rim). The camera then moves 30 m: the clipmap scrolls (toroidal, texel
# snapped to the unjittered view) and the prints stay on their world spots, read from L1 where L0 no longer covers.
# NEEDS the DesertCtl `lua` op (REMAINDER): it runs the text through a ScriptEngine under the open scene's WorldContext.
Дано run Scene "Open Scene FIELD_Barn.desce"
Дано run View "View mode: Deformation Field"
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Position 0,600,900
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0,-0.6,-1
Когда lua "for i = 0, 2 do World.deform{ Stamp = 'DS_CircleRim', At = vector(-150 + i * 150, 0, 0), Params = { Radius = 30 } } end"
Тогда-вид 1_stamp three round prints in a row on the ground in front of the camera, 1.5 m apart, each a blue sink ringed by a red rim; nothing else coloured; editor.log errors 0
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Position 3000,600,900
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Direction -1,-0.2,-0.35
Тогда-вид 2_scrolled from 30 m to the side the same three prints at the same world spots (coarser, L1), no second copy of them elsewhere in view and no shift; editor.log errors 0
